  <!-- ── Step-by-step ─────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="msv__section--dark">
    <div class="msv__container--narrow">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>Step-by-Step NLV Application from London</h2>
        <p>Eight clear steps from deciding to apply to entering Spain on your new visa.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="msv__steps">
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">1</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Check Your Eligibility</h3>
            <p>Confirm you meet the core requirements: passive income of ~€2,400/month (single) or ~€3,000+/month (couple), willingness to live in Spain without working, and no disqualifying criminal record. Use our <a href="https://www.myspanishvisa.com/get-started/" style="color: var(--yellow);">free eligibility check</a> if you are unsure.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">2</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Gather Your Documents</h3>
            <p>Collect all required documents: passport, bank statements (3–6 months), pension letters from DWP or private providers, proof of accommodation in Spain, health insurance certificate, medical certificate, and application form. See the full checklist below.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">3</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Get UK Documents Apostilled</h3>
            <p>Submit all UK documents to the FCDO Legalisation Office (Milton Keynes) for apostille certification. Cost: £75 per document, standard 4–8 week processing. Expedited service available. This is required for all public documents (bank statements, pension letters, ACRO certificate, birth certificate).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">4</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Obtain ACRO Criminal Record Certificate</h3>
            <p>Apply immediately at acro.police.uk (£45 standard, £98 fast-track). This takes 10–15 working days standard. Once received, send it to the FCDO for apostille (included in step 3 if batching), then to a sworn Spanish translator. Start this process as early as possible — it sits on the critical path.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">5</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Arrange Spanish-Authorised Health Insurance</h3>
            <p>Purchase private health insurance from a provider authorised by the Spanish authorities. The policy must have no copayments and provide comprehensive coverage in Spain. EHIC and GHIC cards are not accepted. Annual cost: approximately €700–€2,500 depending on age. Obtain a certificate of coverage to submit with your dossier.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">6</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Book Your BLS London Appointment</h3>
            <p>Once your documents are nearly ready, book your BLS London appointment online. Do not book too far in advance — documents must be recent (bank statements within 3 months). Book 2–4 weeks ahead of when your dossier will be complete.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">7</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Attend BLS Appointment and Submit</h3>
            <p>Attend in person at BLS London with your complete dossier. BLS staff verify completeness and forward to the Spanish consulate. Pay the consulate fee (€80–€150, non-refundable). Receive your tracking reference.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">8</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Wait for Decision, Then Travel to Spain</h3>
            <p>Allow 8–14 weeks from submission. Once approved, collect your stamped passport from BLS London. You then have a window (typically 3 months) to enter Spain. Upon arrival, register at the Extranjería (foreigners' office) within 30 days to obtain your NIE and TIE residency card.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

