  <section class="msv__section--cream">
    <div class="msv__container--narrow">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions — London NLV Applicants</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="msv__faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Do I apply at the Spanish Embassy in London or through BLS?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>You apply through BLS International, not directly at the Spanish Embassy at 39 Chesham Place, London SW1X 8SB. BLS International operates as the authorised visa application centre for Spain in the UK. You submit your documents at BLS London, pay the consulate fee there, and BLS forwards your complete dossier to the relevant Spanish consulate on your behalf. You do not visit the Embassy directly at any stage.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which BLS centre should London applicants use?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>London residents and those in South England, East of England, Wales, and Northern Ireland should use the BLS London centre. Appointments are booked online via the BLS International website. The London centre typically has higher demand than Manchester, so book as early as possible — ideally 4–6 weeks in advance of when your documents will be ready.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is the income requirement for the NLV in 2026?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>The 2026 income threshold is approximately €2,400 per month for a single applicant (based on 400% of the IPREM rate). For a couple, the combined threshold is approximately €3,000–€3,100 per month. Spanish consulates require 3–6 months of bank statements showing consistent passive income from pensions, investments, rental income, or evidence of liquid savings of at least €28,800–€38,000.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need an ACRO certificate for the London NLV application?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. All UK applicants must provide an ACRO Standard Disclosure (Police Certificate) as their criminal record check. It costs £45 standard (10–15 working days) or £98 fast-track (3–5 working days). Apply at acro.police.uk. The certificate must then be apostilled by the FCDO and translated by a sworn Spanish translator before submission at BLS London. Do not substitute with a DBS check — that is a different document and will not be accepted.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How long does the NLV take to process from London?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Processing time from BLS London is typically 8–14 weeks from the date of submission at BLS. London has higher application volumes than Manchester, which can extend processing during peak periods (May to August). Once the consulate makes a decision, BLS notifies you by email and you collect your stamped passport from BLS London in person.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use UK bank statements and pension letters as income proof?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. Spanish consulates accept UK bank statements, DWP State Pension letters, private pension provider statements, and investment income statements from UK financial institutions. However, all documents must be recent (within 3 months at the time of BLS submission), apostilled by the FCDO, and translated into Spanish by a sworn translator. Submit 3–6 months of statements showing consistent passive income deposits to give the strongest possible application.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
